// Title: Potential Cookie Theft via Firefox Remote Debugging on Linux
// Sigma ID: fd321cb2-bf96-4e3a-a908-3ea661ec24a3
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: PersonalRules
// Date: 2026-04-23 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: credential-access, T1539
// Description: Detects the use of the Firefox remote debugging argument which can be abused to steal browser
//   cookies, session data, and credentials. An adversary may launch Firefox with -start-debugger-
//   server to open a debugging port and connect via Remote Debugging Protocol to extract sensitive
//   data.
// False positives:
//   - Developers debugging Firefox extensions or web applications
//   - Automated testing frameworks using Firefox remote debugging
// References:
//   - https://firefox-source-docs.mozilla.org/devtools-user/about_colon_debugging/
//   - https://github.com/wunderwuzzi23/firefox-cookiemonster
//   - https://www.mdsec.co.uk/2022/10/analysing-lastpass-part-1/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/1170f436bbbf22972502a467ac84a05a81d07267/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_browsers_firefox_remote_debugging.yml
